plus the carry-over 1 is 8. \n\nSo putting it all together: 8 (hundred-thousands), 3 (ten-thousands), 0 (thousands), 13 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 5 (ones). But 13 in the hundreds place would be 3 hundreds and 1 carried over to thousands. Wait, but when we added the thousands place, we had 9 + 1 = 10, which gave 0 thousands and 1 carried over. So the thousands place is 0, and the hundreds place is 13. So actually, the digits would be:\n\nHundred-thousands: 8\n\nTen-thousands: 3\n\nThousands: 0\n\nHundreds: 3 (since 13 in the hundreds place is 3 with a carry-over)\n\nTens: 2\n\nOnes: 5\n\nWait, but 13 in the hundreds place would be 3 hundreds and 1 carried over to thousands. But when we added the thousands place, we had 2 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 10, which becomes 0 with a carry-over of 1 to the ten-thousands place. Then the ten-thousands place was 7 + 5 + 1 (carry) = 13, which becomes 3 with a carry-over of 1 to the hundred-thousands place. \n\nSo the digits are:\n\nHundred-thousands: 8\n\nTen-thousands: 3\n\nThousands: 0\n\nHundreds: 3\n\nTens: 2\n\nOnes: 5\n\nSo the total sum is 830,325. Let me verify that. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check by adding the numbers another way. Let's see. \n\n572,811 + 275,514. \n\nBreaking down the numbers:\n\n572,811 = 500,000 + 70,000 + 2,000 + 800 + 10 + 1\n\n275,514 = 200,000 + 70,000 + 5,000 + 500 + 10 + 4\n\nAdding them together:\n\n200,000 + 500,000 = 700,000\n\n70,000 + 70,000 = 140,000\n\n2,000 + 5,000 = 7,000\n\n800 + 500 = 1,300\n\n10 + 10 = 20\n\n1 + 4 = 5\n\nNow add all those together:\n\n700,000 + 140,000 = 840,000\n\n840,000 + 7,000 = 847,000\n\n847,000 + 1,300 = 848,300\n\n848,300 + 20 = 848,320\n\n848,320 + 5 = 848,325\n\nWait, that gives me 848,325. But that contradicts my previous result. Hmm, so which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n572,811: 500,000 + 70,000 + 2,000 + 800 + 10 + 1\n\n275,514: 200,000 + 70,000 + 5,000 + 500 + 10 + 4\n\nAdding:\n\n200,000 (from second number) + 500,000 (from first number) = 700,000\n\n70,000 (from first number) + 70,000 (from second number) = 140,000\n\n2,000 (from first number) + 5,000 (from second number) = 7,000\n\n800 (from first number) + 500 (from second number) = 1,300\n\n10 (from first number) + 10 (from second number) = 20\n\n1 (from first number) + 4 (from second number) = 5\n\nNow adding all these:\n\n700,000 + 140,000 = 840,000\n\n840,000 + 7,000 = 847,000\n\n847,000 + 1,300 = 848,300\n\n848,300 + 20 = 848,320\n\n848,320 + 5 = 848,325\n\nBut when I added the numbers vertically, I got 830,325. There's a discrepancy here. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the vertical addition. Let me try that again.\n\nFirst number: 572,811\n\nSecond number: 275,514\n\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1 + 4 = 5 (ones place)\n\n1 + 1 = 2 (tens place)\n\n8 + 5 = 13 (hundreds place) \u2192 write down 3, carry over 1\n\n2 + 7 = 9, plus the carried 1 = 10 (thousands place) \u2192 write down 0, carry over 1\n\n7 + 5 = 12, plus carried 1 = 13 (ten-thousands place) \u2192 write down 3, carry over 1\n\n5 + 2 = 7, plus carried 1 = 8 (hundred-thousands place)\n\nSo the total is 830,325. But according to the breakdown, it's 848,325. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I added the numbers incorrectly in the breakdown. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 572,811 + 275,514.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 572,811 + 200,000 = 772,811\n\nThen, 772,811 + 70,000 = 842,811\n\n842,811 + 5,000 = 847,811\n\n847,811 + 500 = 848,311\n\n848,311 + 10 = 848,321\n\n848,321 + 4 = 848,325\n\nAh! So here, when adding 500, then 500 again, that's 1,000. Wait, but in the breakdown, 275,514 is 200,000 + 70,000 + 5,000 + 500 + 10 + 4. So 200,000 + 70,000 + 5,000 + 500 is 275,500. Then 10 + 4 is 14. So 572,811 + 275,500 = 848,311. Then 848,311 + 14 = 848,325. So that's correct. \n\nBut when I first did the breakdown, I thought 275,514 is 200,000 + 70,000 + 5,000 + 500 + 10 + 4. So 200,000 + 70,000 is 270,000. Then 270,000 + 5,000 is 275,000. Then 275,000 + 500 is 275,500. Then 275,500 + 10 is 275,510. Then 275,510 + 4 is 275,514. So that's correct. Then adding 572,811 + 275,514. \n\nBut when I added the components, I thought 200,000 + 500,000 = 700,000. Wait, 572,811 is 500,000 + 70,000 + 2,000 + 800 + 10 + 1. So 500,000 + 200,000 = 700,000. Then 70,000 + 70,000 = 140,000. Then 2,000 + 5,000 = 7,000. Then 800 + 500 = 1,300. Then 10 + 10 = 20. Then 1 + 4 = 5. \n\nAdding those components: 700,000 + 140,000 = 840,000. 840,000 + 7,000 = 847,000. 847,000 + 1,300 = 848,300. 848,300 + 20 = 848,320. 848,320 + 5 = 848,325. So that's correct. \n\nBut when I first did the vertical addition, I thought the result was 830,325. That must have been a mistake. Let me check again. \n\nVertical addition:\n\n  572,811\n\n+ 275,514\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1 + 4 = 5\n\n1 + 1 = 2\n\n8 + 5 = 13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\n2 + 7 = 9, plus 1 carried = 10 (write 0, carry 1)\n\n7 + 5 = 12, plus 1 carried = 13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\n5 + 2 = 7, plus 1 carried = 8\n\nSo the sum is 830,325. Wait, but according to the breakdown, it's 848,325. There's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check again step by step.\n\nFirst number: 572,811\n\nSecond number: 275,514\n\nLet me write them aligned properly:\n\n    572,811\n\n  + 275,514\n\n  = ?\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes place: 1 + 4 = 5\n\nTens place: 1 + 1 = 2\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 5 = 13. So write 3, carry 1.\n\nThousands place: 2 + 7 = 9. But we have a carry-over of 1, so 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 7 + 5 = 12. But we have a carry-over of 1, so 12 + 1 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 5 + 2 = 7. But we have a carry-over of 1, so 7 + 1 = 8.\n\nSo the total is 8 (hundred-thousands), 3 (ten-thousands), 0 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 5 (ones). So 830,325.\n\nBut according to the breakdown, it's 848,325. So which is correct?\n\nWait, let me check with another method. Let's use the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nFirst, write the numbers:\n\n    572,811\n\n  + 275,514\n\nStart adding from the right:\n\n1. Ones place: 1 + 4 = 5. Write 5.\n\n2. Tens place: 1 + 1 = 2. Write 2.\n\n3. Hundreds place: 8 + 5 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\n4. Thousands place: 2 + 7 = 9. Add the carried 1: 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n5. Ten-thousands place: 7 + 5 = 12. Add the carried 1: 12 + 1 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\n6. Hundred-thousands place: 5 + 2 = 7. Add the carried 1: 7 + 1 = 8.\n\nSo the sum is 830,325. \n\nBut according to the breakdown, it's 848,325. So which is correct? There must be a mistake here. Let me verify with a calculator.\n\nWait, I don't have a calculator here, but let me try adding the numbers in another way.\n\n572,811 + 275,514.\n\nLet me add 572,811 + 200,000 first. That's 772,811.\n\nThen add 75,514 to 772,811.\n\n772,811 + 75,514.\n\n772,811 + 70,000 = 842,811\n\n842,811 + 5,000 = 847,811\n\n847,811 + 500 = 848,311\n\n848,311 + 14 = 848,325.\n\nSo that's 848,325. But according to vertical addition, it's 830,325. So there's a conflict. Which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 572,811 + 275,514.\n\nLet me write it as:\n\n  572,811\n\n+ 275,514\n\nLet me add the thousands place first. Wait, maybe I need to check each column again.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1 + 4 = 5. Correct.\n\nTens: 1 + 1 = 2. Correct.\n\nHundreds: 8 + 5 = 13. So 3, carry 1. Correct.\n\nThousands: 2 + 7 = 9. Then 9 + 1 (carry) = 10. So 0, carry 1. Correct.\n\nTen-thousands: 7 + 5 = 12. Then 12 + 1 (carry) = 13. So 3, carry 1. Correct.\n\nHundred-thousands: 5 + 2 = 7. Then 7 + 1 (carry) = 8. Correct.\n\nSo the sum is 830,325. But according to the breakdown, it's 848,325. There's a discrepancy of 16,000. Where is the mistake?\n\nWait, let me check the breakdown again. \n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n572,811: 500,000 + 70,000 + 2,000 + 800 + 10 + 1\n\n275,514: 200,000 + 70,000 + 5,000 + 500 + 10 + 4\n\nAdding:\n\n200,000 + 500,000 = 700,000\n\n70,000 + 70,000 = 140,000\n\n2,000 + 5,000 = 7,000\n\n800 + 500 = 1,300\n\n10 + 10 = 20\n\n1 + 4 = 5\n\nAdding all together:\n\n700,000 + 140,000 = 840,000\n\n840,000 + 7,000 = 847,000\n\n847,000 + 1,300 = 848,300\n\n848,300 + 20 = 848,320\n\n848,320 + 5 = 848,325\n\nBut according to vertical addition, it's 830,325. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe the breakdown is wrong. Let me check the components again.\n\nWait, 572,811 is 500,000 + 70,000 + 2,000 + 800 + 10 + 1. That's correct.\n\n275,514 is 200,000 + 70,000 + 5,000 + 500 + 10 + 4. That's also correct.\n\nAdding 200,000 + 500,000 = 700,000. Correct.\n\n70,000 + 70,000 = 140,000. Correct.\n\n2,000 + 5,000 = 7,000. Correct.\n\n800 + 500 = 1,300. Correct.\n\n10 + 10 = 20. Correct.\n\n1 + 4 = 5. Correct.\n\nAdding all components: 700,000 + 140,000 = 840,000. Then 840,000 + 7,000 = 847,000. Then 847,000 + 1,300 = 848,300. Then 848,300 + 20 = 848,320. Then 848,320 + 5 = 848,325. So that's correct.\n\nBut vertical addition gives 830,325. So which is correct? There must be a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nWait, let me check the vertical addition again. Maybe I misaligned the numbers.\n\nFirst number: 572,811\n\nSecond number: 275,514\n\nSo:\n\n    572,811\n\n  + 275,514\n\nLet me write them with commas for clarity:\n\nFirst number: 572,811\n\nSecond number: 275,514\n\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1 (ones) + 4 = 5\n\n1 (tens) + 1 = 2\n\n8 (hundreds) + 5 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n2 (thousands) + 7 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n7 (ten-thousands) + 5 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n5 (hundred-thousands) + 2 = 7 + 1 = 8\n\nSo the sum is 830,325. \n\nBut according to the breakdown, it's 848,325. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check the components again.\n\nWait, 572,811 + 275,514. Let's add them as:\n\n572,811 + 275,514.\n\