14 = 848,325.\n\nSo that's 848,325. But according to vertical addition, it's 830,325. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 572,811 + 275,514.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n    572,811\n\n  + 275,514\n\nLet me add them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1 (ones) + 4 = 5\n\n1 (tens) + 1 = 2\n\n8 (hundreds) + 5 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n2 (thousands) + 7 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n7 (ten-thousands) + 5 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n5 (hundred-thousands) + 2 = 7 + 1 = 8\n\nSo the sum is 830,325. \n\nBut according to the breakdown, it's 848,325. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe the vertical addition is correct. Let me check with another approach. Let's use the difference between the two numbers.\n\n572,811 - 275,514 = ?\n\nIf I subtract, I should get the same difference as 275,514 - 572,811.\n\nBut maybe that's not helpful. Alternatively, let me check if 830,325 + 16,000 = 848,325. So if there's a difference of 16,000, which is 16,000. But why is there a discrepancy?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check each column again.\n\nFirst number: 572,811\n\nSecond number: 275,514\n\nLet me write them as:\n\n    5 7 2 , 8 1 1\n\n  + 2 7 5 , 5 1 4\n\nLet me align them properly:\n\n        572,811\n\n      + 275,514\n\n      = ?\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n1 (ones) + 4 = 5\n\n1 (tens) + 1 = 2\n\n8 (hundreds) + 5 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n2 (thousands) + 7 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n7 (ten-thousands) + 5 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n5 (hundred-thousands) + 2 = 7 + 1 = 8\n\nSo the sum is 830,325. \n\nBut according to the breakdown, it's 848,325. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe the breakdown is wrong. Let me check the components again.\n\nWait, 572,811 + 275,514.\n\nIf I add 572,811 + 275,514, the correct answer should be 848,325. But according to vertical addition, it's 830,325. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mis