it's 1,536,010. So where is the error?\n\nWait, 670,659 +865,351.\n\nWait, 670,659 +865,351. Let's compute this as:\n\n670,659 + 865,351.\n\nLet me add 670,659 + 800,000 =1,470,659.\n\nThen add 65,351: 1,470,659 +65,351.\n\n1,470,659 +60,000 =1,530,659.\n\n1,530,659 +5,000 =1,535,659.\n\n1,535,659 +351 =1,536,010.\n\nYes, that's correct. So the breakdown method must have added an extra 10 somewhere. Wait, in the breakdown, I added 1,400,000 (600k +800k) +130,000 (70k +60k) +5,600 (0,600 +5,000) +350 (50 +300) +10 (9 +1). But 670,659 +865,351 is 670,659 +865,351 =1,536,010. So the breakdown method added 1,400,000 +130,000 +5,600 +350 +10 =1,536,060. But according to the direct addition, it's 1,536,010. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, 670,659 +865,351. Let's compute 670,659 +865,351:\n\nStart with 670,659 +865,351.\n\nLet me add the numbers digit by digit:\n\nUnits:9 +1=10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nTens:5 +5=10 +1=11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nHundreds:6 +3=9 +1=10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nThousands:0 +5=5 +1=6. Write 6, carry 0.\n\nTen-thousands:7 +6=13 +0=13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nHundred-thousands:6 +8=14 +1=15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\nMillions:1.\n\nSo the total is 1,536,010. Therefore, the breakdown method added 1,400,000 +130,000 +5,600 +350 +10 =1,536,060, which is incorrect. So where is the mistake in the breakdown?\n\nWait, 670,659 is 600,000 +70,000 +0,600 +50 +9. So 600,000 +70,000 =670,000. Then +0,600 =670,600. Then +50 =670,650. Then +9 =670,659. Correct.\n\n865,351 is 800,000 +60,000 +5,000 +300 +1. So 800,000 +60,000 =860,000. Then +5,000 =865,000. Then +300 =865,300. Then +1 =865,351. Correct.\n\nAdding the components:\n\n670,659 +865,351 = (600,000 +800,000) + (70,000 +60,000) + (0,600 +5,000) + (50 +300) + (9 +1) =1,400,000 +130,000 +5,600 +350 +10 =1,536,060. But according to the direct addition, it's 1,536,010. So there's a discrepancy of 50. Where is the mistake?\n\nWait, 670,659 +865,351. Let's compute 670,659 +865,351:\n\n670,659 +865,351.\n\nLet me compute 