ands: 5,000\n\n- 3 hundreds: 300\n\n- 3 tens: 30\n\n- 4 ones: 4\n\nSo 500,000 + 5,000 + 300 + 30 + 4 = 505,334. Right. So my breakdown was correct. Then 460,020 is 400,000 + 60,000 + 20. So 400,000 + 60,000 = 460,000. Then +20. So 460,020. So adding 505,334 + 460,020. \n\nBut when I do the breakdown method, I get 965,520, but column addition gives 965,354. So which is correct? Let me check with another method. Let's compute 505,334 + 460,020 using another approach, like the standard algorithm.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 0 = 4\n\n3 + 2 = 5\n\n3 + 0 = 3\n\n5 + 0 = 5\n\n0 + 6 = 6\n\n5 + 4 = 9\n\nSo the sum is 965,354. Therefore, the column addition is correct. Then why does the breakdown method give a different answer? Because in the breakdown method, I must have added incorrectly. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal breakdown:\n\n505,334 = 500,000 + 5,000 + 500 + 30 + 4\n\n460,020 = 400,000 + 60,000 + 20\n\nAdding the 500,000 + 400,000 = 900,000\n\n5,000 + 60,000 = 65,000\n\n500 + 20 = 520\n\nThen 900,000 + 65,000 = 965,000\n\n965,000 + 520 = 965,520\n\nBut according to column addition, it's 965,354. So where is the mistake here?\n\nWait, 500,000 + 400,000 is 900,000. Then 5,000 + 60,000 is 65,000. Then 500 + 20 is 520. So 900,000 + 65,000 is 965,000. Then 965,000 + 520 is 965,520. But according to the column addition, it's 965,354. So there's a difference of 170. \n\nWait, maybe I added 500 + 20 incorrectly? 500 + 20 is 520. That's correct. Then 965,000 + 520 is 965,520. But according to the column addition, it's 965,354. So where is the error?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the breakdown of the original numbers. Let me check 505,334 again. 505,334: 500,000 + 5,000 + 300 + 30 + 4. Wait, 500,000 + 5,000 is 505,000. Then 300 + 30 is 330. Then 4. So 505,000 + 330 + 4 = 505,334. Correct. Then 460,020: 400,000 + 60,000 + 20. 400,000 + 60,000 is 460,000. Then +20. So 460,020. Correct. So adding 505,334 + 460,020. \n\nBut according to column addition, the sum is 9