own: 11 (hundred-thousands), 7 (ten-thousands), 1 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 6 (ones). So 117,876. \n\nBut when I broke it down into components, I got 1,138,876. Which is a big difference. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the components. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n731,130: \n\n- 700,000\n\n- 30,000\n\n- 1,000\n\n- 100\n\n- 30\n\n407,746:\n\n- 400,000\n\n- 7,000\n\n- 700\n\n- 40\n\n- 6\n\nAdding the thousands place: 1,000 + 7,000 = 8,000. Correct.\n\nHundreds place: 1,000 + 700 = 1,700. Correct.\n\nTens place: 100 + 40 = 140. Correct.\n\nOnes place: 30 + 6 = 36. Correct.\n\nNow, adding all components:\n\n700,000 + 400,000 = 1,100,000\n\n1,000 + 7,000 = 8,000\n\n1,000 + 700 = 1,700\n\n100 + 40 = 140\n\n30 + 6 = 36\n\nNow, adding these together:\n\n1,100,000 + 8,000 = 1,108,000\n\n1,108,000 + 1,700 = 1,110,700\n\n1,110,700 + 140 = 1,110,840\n\n1,110,840 + 36 = 1,110,876\n\nWait, so according to this, the total is 1,110,876. But when I added vertically, I got 117,876. That's a huge difference. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me try adding the numbers again vertically, step by step.\n\nFirst number: 731,130\n\nSecond number: 407,746\n\nAdding:\n\n731,130\n\n+407,746\n\nLet's write them one under the other:\n\n  731130\n\n+ 407746\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n0 + 6 = 6 (ones place)\n\n3 + 4 = 7 (tens)\n\n1 + 7 = 8 (hundreds)\n\n1 + 0 = 1 (thousands)\n\n3 + 4 = 7 (ten-thousands)\n\n7 + 4 = 11 (hundred-thousands)\n\nSo the sum is 117,876. But according to the component method, it's 1,110,876. There's a discrepancy of 1,110,876 - 117,876 = 993,000. That's a lot. So clearly, one of the methods is wrong. \n\nWait, maybe I messed up the component breakdown. Let me check again. \n\nWait, 731,130 is 700,000 + 30,000 + 1,000 + 100 + 30. That's correct. \n\n407,746 is 400,000 + 7,000 + 700 + 40 + 6. That's also correct. \n\nAdding the thousands place: 1,000 + 7,000 = 8,000. 