ligned the digits. Let me write both numbers with leading spaces:\n\n731,130\n\n+407,746\n\nLet's write them aligned properly:\n\n      731,130\n\n    +407,746\n\nNow, adding each column:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 +6 =6\n\n3 +4 =7\n\n1 +7 =8\n\n1 +0 =1\n\n3 +4 =7\n\n7 +4 =11\n\nSo the sum is 117,876. But according to the component method, it's 1,138,876. Which is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with a calculator. Let me compute 731,130 + 407,746. \n\nFirst, 731,130 + 400,000 = 1,131,130\n\nThen, 1,131,130 +7,746 = 1,138,876. \n\nAh! So the component method was correct. The vertical addition was wrong. \n\nWait, why did the vertical addition give 117,876? That's way too small. Let me check again. \n\nWait, 731,130 + 407,746. Let's add them as 731,130 + 400,000 = 1,131,130. Then add the remaining 7,746: 1,131,130 +7,746. \n\n1,131,130 +7,000 =1,138,130\n\n1,138,130 +746 =1,138,876. \n\nYes, that's correct. So the vertical addition must have had a mistake. \n\nWait, when I did the vertical addition earlier, I wrote:\n\n731,130\n\n+407,746\n\nAnd added the digits as:\n\n11 (hundred-thousands), 7 (ten-thousands), 1 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 6 (ones). \n\nBut 731,130 is 7 hundred thirty-one thousand one hundred thirty, and 407,746 is four hundred seven thousand seven hundred forty-six. Adding those together, the result should be 1,138,876. \n\nBut when I added the digits column by column, I got 117,876. That's clearly wrong. \n\nWait, maybe I misaligned the digits. Let me write them out:\n\n      731,130\n\n    +407,746\n\nBut if I write them aligned properly:\n\n        731,130\n\n      +407,746\n\nBut in vertical addition, we need to make sure the digits are aligned by place value. So:\n\n        731,130\n\n      +407,746\n\nWhich is:\n\n7 3 1 1 3 0\n\n+4 0 7 7 4 6\n\nBut when adding, we should align them as:\n\nHundreds of thousands | Ten thousands | Thousands | Hundreds | Tens | Ones\n\nSo:\n\n      7 3 1 1 3 0\n\n    +4 0 7 7 4 6\n\nBut in vertical addition, we need to line them up:\n\n        731,130\n\n      +407,746\n\nWhich would be:\n\n731,130\n\n+407,746\n\nSo breaking down:\n\nHundreds of thousands: 7 and 4\n\nTen thousands: 3 and 0\n\nThousands: 1 and 7\n\nHundreds: 1 and 0\n\nTens: 3 and 4\n\nOnes: 0 and 6\n\nSo adding each column:\n\nOnes: 0 +6 =6\n\nTens:3 +4 =7\n\nHundreds:1 +0 =1\n\nThousands:1 +7 =8\n\nTen thousands:3 +0 =3\n\nHundred thousands:7 +4 =11\n\nSo the sum is 1138876. Wait, but written as 117,876. Wait, no. Wait, 11 (hundred thousands) 7 (ten thousands) 1 (thousands) 8 (hundreds) 7 (tens) 6 (ones). So 117,876. But according to the component method, it's 1,138,876. \n\nWait, this is a problem. There's a mistake here. How can two different methods give different results? \n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the component method. Let me check again. \n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n731,130: 700,000 +30,000 +1,000 +100 +30\n\n407,746:400,000 +7,000 +700 +40 +6\n\nAdding components:\n\n700,000 +400,000 =1,100,000\n\n30,000 +7,000 =37,000\n\n1,000 +700 =1,700\n\n100 +40 =140\n\n30 +6 =36\n\nAdding all components:\n\n1,100,000 +37,000 =1,137,000\n\n1,137,000 +1,700 =1,138,700\n\n1,138,700 +140 =1,138,840\n\n1,138,840 +36 =1,138,876\n\nYes, that's correct. So the component method gives 1,138,876. The vertical addition gives 117,876. So there's a mistake in the vertical addition. \n\nWait, but when I added the vertical digits, I got 117,876. But according to the component method, it's 1,138,876. Which is correct? \n\nWait, let's check with a calculator. Let me compute 731,130 + 407,746. \n\nFirst, 731,130 + 400,000 = 1,131,130\n\nThen, 1,131,130 +7,746 = 1,138,876. \n\nYes, that's correct. So the vertical addition must have had a mistake. \n\nWait, how did I get 117,876 before? Let me check again. \n\nWait, perhaps I added the numbers incorrectly. Let me write them out:\n\n731,130\n\n+407,746\n\nIf I add these numbers digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 +6 =6\n\n3 +4 =7\n\n1 +7 =8\n\n1 +0 =1\