, 30,000 is 3, 1,000 is 1, 100 is 1, 10 is 1, 1 is 1. So total 5+3+1+1+1+1=12. Wait, but 500,000 + 30,000 + 1,000 + 100 + 10 + 1 = 531,111. So that's correct.\n\nBreaking down 818,308:\n\n- 800,000\n\n- 10,000\n\n- 8,000\n\n- 300\n\n- 0\n\n- 8\n\nSo, 800,000 + 10,000 + 8,000 + 300 + 0 + 8 = 818,308. Correct.\n\nAdding the components:\n\nMillions: 500,000 + 800,000 = 1,300,000\n\nHundred thousands: 30,000 + 10,000 = 40,000\n\nTen thousands: 1,000 + 8,000 = 9,000\n\nThousands: 100 + 300 = 400\n\nHundreds: 10 + 0 = 10\n\nTens: 10 + 8 = 18\n\nOnes: 1 + 8 = 9\n\nAdding all these together:\n\n1,300,000 + 40,000 = 1,340,000\n\n1,340,000 + 9,000 = 1,349,000\n\n1,349,000 + 400 = 1,349,400\n\n1,349,400 + 10 = 1,349,410\n\n1,349,410 + 18 = 1,349,428\n\nBut according to vertical addition, it's 1,349,419. So there's a discrepancy of 9. Where is the mistake?\n\nWait, maybe in the vertical addition, the thousands place was miscalculated. Let's check again:\n\nVertical addition:\n\n  531,111\n\n+ 818,308\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1 + 8 = 9\n\nTens: 1 + 0 = 1\n\nHundreds: 1 + 3 = 4\n\nThousands: 1 + 8 = 9\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 1 = 4\n\nHundred-thousands: 5 + 8 = 13 (write down 3, carry over 1)\n\nSo, the total is 1,349,419.\n\nBut when adding components, it's 1,349,428. So, which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the component addition. Let's check:\n\nWait, 531,111 + 818,308.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 531,111 + 800,000 = 1,331,111\n\nThen, add 18,308: 1,331,111 + 18,308.\n\n1,331,111 + 10,000 = 1,341,111\n\n1,341,111 + 8,000 = 1,349,111\n\n1,349,111 + 300 = 1,349,411\n\n1,349,411 + 8 = 1,349,419.\n\nAh! There we go. So when adding step by step, it's 1,349,419. So where did I go wrong in the component method?\n\nWait, in the component method, I added:\n\n1,300,000 (millions) + 40,000 (hundred thousands) = 1,340,000\n\n1,340,000 + 9,000 (ten thousands) = 1,349,000\n\n1,349,000 + 400 (thousands) = 1,349,400\n\n1,349,400 + 10 (hundreds) = 1,349,