0 + 18,000 = 88,000\n\n684 + 419 = 1,103\n\nNow, adding those together: 1,000,000 + 88,000 = 1,088,000. Then 1,088,000 + 1,103 = 1,089,103. Wait, that's different. Wait, hold on. Wait, 684 + 419. Let me check that again.\n\n684 + 419. 600 + 400 = 1,000. 80 + 10 = 90. 4 + 9 = 13. So, 1,000 + 90 + 13 = 1,103. Yes, that's correct. Then 1,000,000 + 88,000 is 1,088,000. Then 1,088,000 + 1,103. Let's add 1,088,000 + 1,000 = 1,089,000. Then add 103: 1,089,000 + 103 = 1,089,103. Wait, but earlier when adding step by step, I got 1,089,003. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n670,684: 600,000 + 70,000 + 600 + 80 + 4.\n\n418,419: 400,000 + 10,000 + 8,000 + 400 + 10 + 9.\n\nAdding them:\n\n600,000 + 400,000 = 1,000,000\n\n70,000 + 10,000 = 80,000\n\n600 + 8,000 = 8,600\n\n80 + 400 = 480\n\n80 + 10 = 90\n\n4 + 9 = 13\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, when breaking down 670,684, it's 600,000 + 70,000 + 600 + 80 + 4. So, 600,000 + 70,000 is 670,000. Then 600 + 80 + 4 is 684. Similarly, 418,419 is 400,000 + 10,000 + 8,000 + 400 + 10 + 9. So, 400,000 + 10,000 is 410,000. Then 8,000 + 400 is 8,400. Then 10 + 9 is 19. So, total is 670,000 + 410,000 = 1,080,000. Then 684 + 8,400 + 19. 684 + 8,400 is 9,084. Then 9,084 + 19 = 9,103. So total sum is 1,080,000 + 9,103 = 1,089,103. Wait, but earlier when adding step by step, I got 1,089,003. So which is correct?\n\nWait, there's a conflict here. Let me check the original addition again. Let's do it digit by digit.\n\n670,684\n\n+418,419\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 9 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\n8 (tens place) + 1 (from 418,419) = 9, plus the carried 1 is 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n6 (hundreds place) + 4 (from 418,419) = 10, plus carried 1 is 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\n7 (thousands place) + 8 (from 418,419) = 15, plus carried 1 is 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\n0 (ten-thousands place) + 1 (from 418,419) = 1, plus carried 1 is 2. Write 2.\n\n6 (hundred-thousands place) + 4 (from 418,419) = 10. Write 0, carry 1. So the final digit is 1.\n\nSo total is 1,089,003. But when breaking down into thousands, I got 1,089,103. There's a difference of 900. Where is the mistake?\n\nWait, let's check the breakdown again. If 670,684 is 600,000 + 70,000 + 600 + 80 + 4, and 418,419 is 400,000 + 10,000 + 8,000 + 400 + 10 + 9. Then adding:\n\n600,000 + 400,000 = 1,000,000\n\n70,000 + 10,000 = 80,000\n\n600 + 8,000 = 8,600\n\n80 + 400 = 480\n\n80 + 10 = 90\n\n4 + 9 = 13\n\nAdding those together:\n\n1,000,000 + 80,000 = 1,080,000\n\n1,080,000 + 8,600 = 1,088,600\n\n1,088,600 + 480 = 1,089,080\n\n1,089,080 + 90 = 1,089,170\n\n1,089,170 + 13 = 1,089,183\n\nWait, that's different. Wait, this is getting confusing. Let me check each step again.\n\nOriginal breakdown:\n\n670,684 = 600,000 + 70,000 + 600 + 80 + 4\n\n418,419 = 400,000 + 10,000 + 8,000 + 400 + 10 + 9\n\nAdding:\n\n600,000 + 400,000 = 1,000,000\n\n70,000 + 10,000 = 80,000\n\n600 + 8,000 = 8,600\n\n80 + 400 = 480\n\n80 + 10 = 90\n\n4 + 9 = 13\n\nNow, adding these results:\n\n1,000,000 (from 600k + 400k)\n\n+80,000 (from 70k +10k) = 1,080,000\n\n+8,600 (from 600 +8,000) = 1,088,600\n\n+480 (from 80 +400) = 1,089,080\n\n+90 (from 80 +10) = 1,089,170\n\n+13 (from 4 +9) = 1,089,183\n\nWait, so according to this breakdown, the sum is 1,089,183. But when adding digit by digit, I got 1,089,003. There's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, this is a problem. Let me check with another method. Let's use the standard addition method again.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n  670,684\n\n+ 418,419\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n4 + 9 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\n8 (tens place) + 1 (from the second number) = 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n6 (hundreds place) + 4 (from the second number) = 10 + 1 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\n7 (thousands place) + 8 (from the second number) = 15 + 1 = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\n0 (ten-thousands place) + 1 (from the second number) = 1 + 1 = 2. Write 2, no carry.\n\n6 (hundred-thousands place) + 4 (from the second number) = 10. Write 0, carry 1. So total is 10 in the hundred-thousands place.\n\nSo the sum is 1,089,003. But according to the breakdown, it's 1,089,183. There's a discrepancy of 900. Where is the mistake?\n\nWait, let's check the breakdown again. If 670,684 is 600,000 + 70,000 + 600 + 80 + 4, and 418,419 is 400,000 + 10,000 + 8,000 + 400 + 10 + 9. Then adding:\n\n600,000 + 400,000 = 1,000,000\n\n70,000 + 10,000 = 80,000\n\n600 + 8,000 = 8,600\n\n80 + 400 = 480\n\n80 + 10 = 90\n\n4 + 9 = 13\n\nAdding these:\n\n1,000,000 + 80,000 = 1,080,000\n\n1,080,000 + 8,600 = 1,088,600\n\n1,088,600 + 480 = 1,089,080\n\n1,089,080 + 90 = 1,089,170\n\n1,089,170 + 13 = 1,089,183\n\nWait, but according to the digit-by-digit addition, the sum is 1,089,003. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let's check the original numbers again.\n\n670,684: Let's verify. 600,000 + 70,000 = 670,000. Then 684. So 670,000 + 684 = 670,684. Correct.\n\n418,419: 400,000 + 18,000 = 418,000. Then 419. So 418,000 + 419 = 418,419. Correct.\n\nSo the breakdown is correct. Then why the discrepancy?\n\nWait, perhaps when adding the components, I missed a comma or a digit. Let's check the digit-by-digit addition again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n670,684\n\n+418,419\n\nLet me write them out with commas for clarity:\n\n670,684\n\n+418,419\n\nAdding each digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 9 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\n8 (tens place) + 1 (from the second number) = 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n6 (hundreds place) + 4 (from the second number) = 10 + 1 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\n7 (thousands place) + 8 (from the second number) = 15 + 1 = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\n0 (ten-thousands place) + 1 (from the second number) = 1 + 1 = 2. Write 2, no carry.\n\n6 (hundred-thousands place) + 4 (from the second number) = 10. Write 0, carry 1. So total is 10 in the hundre