,810 + 173,875.\n\nAlternatively, break down each number into thousands, hundreds, tens, etc.\n\nFirst number: 805,810.\n\n805,810 = 800,000 + 5,000 + 800 + 10.\n\n173,875 = 100,000 + 70,000 + 3,000 + 800 + 70 + 5.\n\nAdding them:\n\n100,000 + 200,000 = 300,000\n\n70,000 + 50,000 = 120,000\n\n5,000 + 3,000 = 8,000\n\n800 + 800 = 1,600\n\n10 + 70 = 80\n\n0 + 5 = 5\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n300,000 + 120,000 = 420,000\n\n420,000 + 8,000 = 428,000\n\n428,000 + 1,600 = 429,600\n\n429,600 + 80 = 429,680\n\n429,680 + 5 = 429,685\n\nWait, so that gives 429,685. But that contradicts the previous result. Hmm, so which one is correct?\n\nWait, this is confusing. Let me check with actual addition.\n\nWait, 805,810 + 173,875.\n\nLet me compute 805,810 + 173,875.\n\nAlternatively, 805,810 + 173,875.\n\nLet me add 805,810 + 100,000 = 905,810\n\nThen add 70,000: 905,810 + 70,000 = 975,810\n\nThen add 3,000: 975,810 + 3,000 = 978,810\n\nThen add 800: 978,810 + 800 = 979,610\n\nThen add 70: 979,610 + 70 = 979,680\n\nThen add 5: 979,680 + 5 = 979,685.\n\nWait, so that's 979,685. But when I broke it down into thousands, I got 429,685. That can't be. There's a mistake here.\n\nWait, no. Wait, when I broke down 805,810 into 800,000 + 5,000 + 800 + 10, and 173,875 into 100,000 + 70,000 + 3,000 + 800 + 70 + 5, then adding those components:\n\n100,000 + 70,000 = 170,000\n\n200,000 + 50,000 = 250,000\n\n5,000 + 3,000 = 8,000\n\n800 + 800 = 1,600\n\n10 + 70 = 80\n\n5 = 5\n\nAdding those:\n\n170,000 + 250,000 = 420,000\n\n420,000 + 8,000 = 428,000\n\n428,000 + 1,600 = 429,600\n\n429,600 + 80 = 429,680\n\n429,680 + 5 = 429,685\n\nBut this contradicts the direct addition. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the breakdown. Let's check:\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n805,810: 800,000 + 5,000 + 800 + 10. That's correct.\n\n173,875: 100,000 + 70,000 + 3,000 + 800 + 70 + 5. That's also correct.\n\nAdding the thousands components:\n\n800 (from first number) + 800 (from second numbe