 (tens) + 0 = 2\n\n2 (hundreds) + 4 = 6\n\n7 (thousands) + 0 = 7\n\n4 (ten-thousands) + 8 = 12. So write down 2, carry over 1.\n\n4 (hundred-thousands) + 5 = 9, plus the carried 1 is 10.\n\nSo the total is 109,762. But when I broke it down, I got 534,401. That can't be right. There's a mistake here. \n\nWait, hold on. If I break down 447,222 as 400,000 + 40,000 + 7,000 + 200 + 20 + 2, and 580,401 as 500,000 + 80,000 + 0 + 400 + 0 + 1, then adding the ten-thousands place: 40,000 + 80,000 = 120,000. Then 400,000 + 120,000 = 520,000. Then the thousands place: 7,000 + 0 = 7,000. Then 520,000 + 7,000 = 527,000. Then hundreds, tens, ones: 200 + 400 + 1 = 601. So 527,000 + 601 = 527,601. Wait, that's different from before. Wait, maybe I messed up the breakdown earlier.\n\nWait, let's check again. 447,222 is 400,000 + 40,000 + 7,000 + 200 + 20 + 2. So 400k + 40k = 440k, plus 7k = 447k. Then 400k + 40k = 440k, plus 7k = 447k. Then 400k + 40k = 440k, plus 7k = 447k. Wait, no, that's not right. Wait, 447,222 is 400,000 + 40,000 + 7,000 + 200 + 20 + 2. So 400k + 40k is 440k, plus 7k is 447k. Then 400k + 40k is 440k, plus 7k is 447k. Then 400k + 40k is 440k, plus 7k is 447k. Wait, no, that's not correct. Wait, 447,222 is 400,000 + 40,000 + 7,000 + 200 + 20 + 2. So 400k + 40k = 440k, plus 7k = 447k. Then 400k + 40k = 440k, plus 7k = 447k. Then 400k + 40k = 440k, plus 7k = 447k. Wait, that seems like adding 400k + 40k + 40k + 40k, which is 440k. But 447,222 is 447,000 + 222. So maybe my breakdown is wrong. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 447,222: 400,000 + 40,000 + 7,000 + 200 + 20 + 2. So 400k + 40k = 440k, plus 7k = 447k. Then 400k + 40k = 440k, plus 7k = 447k. Then 400k + 40k = 440k, plus 7k = 447k. Wait, that's 447k + 40k = 487k. Wait, no, I think I'm getting confused here. Let me write it out step by step.\n\nOriginal number: 447,222\n\nBreakdown:\n\n- 400,000 (hundred thousands)\n- 40,000 (ten thousands)\n- 7,000 (thousands)\n- 200 (hundreds)\n- 20 (tens)\n- 2 (ones)\n\nSo adding those: 400,000 + 40,000 = 440,000\n\n440,000 + 7,000 = 447,000\n\n447,000 + 200 = 447,200\n\n447,200 + 20 = 447,220\n\n447,220 + 2 = 447,222. Correct.\n\nSimilarly, 580,401:\n\n- 500,000 (hundred thousands)\n- 80,000 (ten thousands)\n- 0 (thousands)\n- 400 (hundreds)\n- 0 (tens)\n- 1 (ones)\n\nAdding those: 500,000 + 80,000 = 580,000\n\n580,000 + 0 = 580,000\n\n580,000 + 400 = 580,400\n\n580,400 + 0 = 580,400\n\n580,400 + 1 = 580,401. Correct.\n\nNow, adding the two broken parts:\n\n447,000 + 580,000 = 1,027,000\n\nThen 220 + 401 = 621\n\nSo total is 1,027,000 + 621 = 1,027,621\n\nWait, that's different from both previous results. Now I'm really confused. What's going on here?\n\nWait, hold on. Let me check this again. If 447,222 is broken into 400,000 + 40,000 + 7,000 + 200 + 20 + 2, and 580,401 is 500,000 + 80,000 + 0 + 400 + 0 + 1, then adding the ten-thousands place: 40,000 + 80,000 = 120,000. Then 400,000 + 120,000 = 520,000. Then thousands place: 7,000 + 0 = 7,000. Then 520,000 + 7,000 = 527,000. Then hundreds, tens, ones: 200 + 400 + 1 = 601. Then 527,000 + 601 = 527,601. But when I added the two broken parts earlier, I got 1,027,621. Which is conflicting. \n\nWait, now I realize the mistake. When I broke down 447,222 as 400,000 + 40,000 + 7,000 + 200 + 20 + 2, that's correct. Similarly, 580,401 is 500,000 + 80,000 + 0 + 400 + 0 + 1. So adding the ten-thousands place: 40,000 + 80,000 = 120,000. Then 400,000 + 120,000 = 520,000. Then thousands place: 7,000 + 0 = 7,000. Then 520,000 + 7,000 = 527,000. Then hundreds, tens, ones: 200 + 400 + 1 = 601. Then 527,000 + 601 = 527,601. But when I added the two numbers directly, I got 109,762. That can't be. There's a mistake here. \n\nWait, no. Wait, 447,222 and 580,401. Let me add them using another method. Let's use the column addition again step by step.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 (ones) + 1 = 3\n\n2 (tens) + 0 = 2\n\n2 (hundreds) + 4 = 6\n\n7 (thousands) + 0 = 7\n\n4 (ten-thousands) + 8 = 12. So write down