usands, thousands, hundreds, tens, ones)\n\nSo when adding:\n\nHundreds place: 4 (from first number) and 7 (from second number). 4 + 7 = 11. So we write 1 and carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 3 (from first number) and 5 (from second number). 3 + 5 = 8. But we had a carryover of 1, so total is 8 + 1 = 9. So write down 9, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place: 9 (from first number) and 8 (from second number). 9 + 8 = 17. No carryover? Wait, 9 + 8 is 17. So we write down 7 and carry over 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 6 (from first number) and 1 (from second number). 6 + 1 = 7. But we had a carryover of 1 from the ten thousands place. So total is 7 + 1 = 8. Write down 8.\n\nSo putting it all together: 8 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 2 (ones). So the sum is 879,172.\n\nWait, let me verify that again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 8 + 4 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nTens: 5 + 1 = 6. Add carryover 1: 7.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 7 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 3 + 5 = 8. Add carryover 1: 9.\n\nTen thousands: 9 + 8 = 17. Write 7, carry 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 6 + 1 = 7. Add carryover 1: 8.\n\nSo the sum is 879,172. Let me check with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking down the numbers:\n\n693,458 + 185,714.\n\nLet's add 693,458 + 100,000 = 793,458\n\nThen add 80,000: 793,458 + 80,000 = 873,458\n\nThen add 5,000: 873,458 + 5,000 = 878,458\n\nThen add 700: 878,458 + 700 = 879,158\n\nThen add 10: 879,158 + 10 = 879,168\n\nThen add 4: 879,168 + 4 = 879,172.\n\nYes, that matches. So the sum is 879,172.\n\nAlternatively, using column addition again:\n\n  693,458\n+ 185,714\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 + 4 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\n5 + 1 = 6 + 1 = 7.\n\n4 + 7 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\n3 + 5 = 8 + 1 = 9.\n\n9 + 8 = 17. Write 7, carry 1.\n\n6 + 1 = 7 + 1 = 8.\n\nSo the result is 879,172. That seems consistent.\n\nWait, just to be thorough,