n 11 * 100,000 = 1,100,000. Then the ten thousands place is 13, which is 13 * 10,000 = 130,000. Then thousands place 9 * 1,000 = 9,000. Hundreds place 6 * 100 = 600. Tens place 9 * 10 = 90. Units 9. So adding all together:\n\n1,100,000 + 130,000 = 1,230,000\n\n1,230,000 + 9,000 = 1,239,000\n\n1,239,000 + 600 = 1,239,600\n\n1,239,600 + 90 = 1,239,690\n\n1,239,690 + 9 = 1,239,699\n\nSo the total is 1,239,699. But earlier, when I did the step-by-step addition, I got 1,131,599. Which is different. So there must be a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nWait, let's check the step-by-step addition again. Maybe I messed up the numbers.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n991,841\n\n139,758\n\nStep-by-step addition:\n\nFirst, 991,841 + 100,000 = 1,091,841\n\nThen, 1,091,841 + 30,000 = 1,121,841\n\n1,121,841 + 9,000 = 1,130,841\n\n1,130,841 + 700 = 1,131,541\n\n1,131,541 + 50 = 1,131,591\n\n1,131,591 + 8 = 1,131,599\n\nBut according to the column addition, it's 1,239,699. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the step-by-step addition. Let me check each step again.\n\nFirst step: 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. Let's compute 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000. 991,841 + 100,000