 them with commas for clarity:\n\n348,757  \n+450,167  \n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 (ones) + 7 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1.\n\n5 (tens) + 6 = 11 + 1 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1.\n\n8 (hundreds) + 0 = 8 + 1 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 0.\n\n4 (thousands) + 1 = 5 \u2192 5, carry 0.\n\n3 (ten-thousands) + 4 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0.\n\n0 (hundred-thousands) + 0 = 0 + 0 = 0.\n\nSo the total is 798,924? Wait, let me check again. Wait, 348,757 + 450,167. Let me add the numbers step by step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking them into parts:\n\n348,757 is 300,000 + 40,000 + 8,000 + 700 + 50 + 7.\n\n450,167 is 400,000 + 50,000 + 0 + 1,000 + 60 + 7.\n\nAdding them:\n\n300,000 + 400,000 = 700,000\n\n40,000 + 50,000 = 90,000\n\n8,000 + 0 = 8,000\n\n700 + 1,000 = 1,700\n\n50 + 60 = 110\n\n7 + 7 = 14\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n700,000 + 90,000 = 790,000\n\n790,000 + 8,000 = 798,000\n\n798,000 + 1,700 = 799,700\n\n799,700 + 110 = 799,810\n\n799,810 + 14 = 799,824\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result. Hmm. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, when I added the columns step by step before, I got 798,924. But when breaking into parts, I got 799,824. There must be a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nLet me check the column addition again.\n\nFirst, aligning the numbers:\n\n   348,757  \n+ 450,167  \n------------\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 7 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1.\n\n5 + 6 = 11 + 1 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1.\n\n8 + 0 = 8 + 1 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 0.\n\n4 + 1 = 5 \u2192 5, carry 0.\n\n3 + 4 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0.\n\n0 + 0 = 0 \u2192 0.\n\nSo the sum is 798,924. But when breaking into parts, I got 799,824. There's a discrepancy here. Which is correct?\n\nWait, let's check the breakdown again. Maybe I made a mistake there.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n348,757: 300,000 + 40,000 + 8,000 + 700 + 50 + 7.\n\n450,167: 400,000 + 50,000 + 0 + 1,000 + 60 + 7.\n\nAdding:\n\n300,000 + 400,000 = 700,000\n\n40,000 + 50,000 = 90,000\n\n8,000 + 0 = 8,000\n\n700 + 1,000 = 1,700\n\n50 + 60 = 110\n\n7 + 7 = 14\n\nNow adding these:\n\n700,000 + 90,000 = 790,000\n\n790,000 + 8,000 = 798,000\n\n798,000 + 1,700 = 799,700\n\n799,700 + 110 = 799,810\n\n799,810 + 14 = 799,824\n\nWait, so according to this, the total is 799,824. But according to the column addition, it's 798,924. There's a difference of 799,824 - 798,924 = 900. Hmm, so where is the mistake?\n\nWait, let's check the column addition again. Let me write down the numbers vertically:\n\n    348,757  \n  + 450,167  \n  ------------\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n7 (ones) + 7 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1.\n\nTens place: 5 + 6 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1.\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 0 = 8 + 1 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 0.\n\nThousands place: 4 + 1 = 5 \u2192 5, carry 0.\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 + 4 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 + 0 = 0.\n\nSo the sum is 798,924. But according to the breakdown, it's 799,824. There's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check the breakdown again. Let's take the numbers:\n\n348,757: 300,000 + 40,000 + 8,000 + 700 + 50 + 7.\n\n450,167: 400,000 + 50,000 + 0 + 1,000 + 60 + 7.\n\nAdding:\n\n300,000 + 400,000 = 700,000\n\n40,000 + 50,000 = 90,000\n\n8,000 + 0 = 8,000\n\n700 + 1,000 = 1,700\n\n50 + 60 = 110\n\n7 + 7 = 14\n\nAdding these:\n\n700,000 + 90,000 = 790,000\n\n790,000 + 8,000 = 798,000\n\n798,000 + 1,700 = 799,700\n\n799,700 + 110 = 799,810\n\n799,810 + 14 = 799,824\n\nWait, so according to this, the total is 799,824. But according to the column addition, it's 798,924. There's a difference of 900. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the column addition. Let me check that again.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n    348,757  \n  + 450,167  \n  ------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 7 + 7 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nTens place: 5 + 6 = 11 + 1 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 0 = 8 + 1 = 9. Write 9, carry 0.\n\nThousands place: 4 + 1 = 5. Wri