lts:\n\n300,000 + 110,000 = 410,000\n\n410,000 + 11,000 = 421,000\n\n421,000 + 1,000 = 422,000\n\n422,000 + 50 = 422,050\n\n422,050 + 14 = 422,064\n\nYep, same result. So that seems right. Alternatively, maybe using another addition technique. Let's try adding 243,229 + 178,835 by rounding numbers to make them easier.\n\n243,229 is close to 240,000. 178,835 is close to 180,000. 240,000 + 180,000 = 420,000. Then adjust for the extra 3,229 and 1,165. So 420,000 + 3,229 + 1,165. 3,229 + 1,165 = 4,394. Then 420,000 + 4,394 = 424,394. Wait, that's different. Hmm, did I do that right?\n\nWait, 243,229 is 240,000 + 3,229. 178,835 is 180,000 - 1,165. So adding them together: 240,000 + 180,000 = 420,000. Then subtract the 1,165 from the 3,229? Wait, no. Wait, if 178,835 is 180,000 - 1,165, then adding 243,229 + 178,835 is 243,229 + (180,000 - 1,165) = 243,229 + 180,000 - 1,165. So 243,229 + 180,000 = 423,229. Then subtract 1,165: 423,229 - 1,165. Let's compute that.\n\n423,229 - 1,000 = 422,229\n\n422,229 - 165 = 422,064. \n\nAh, there we go. So that method also gives 422,064. So that's consistent. So seems like 422,064 is the correct answer. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, but I can check with another method. Let's do column addition again step by step.\n\nFirst number: 243,229\n\nSecond number: 178,835\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n  243229\n\n+ 178835\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n9 + 5 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\n2 + 3 = 5, plus 1 is 6. Write 6, no carry.\n\n3 + 8 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\n4 + 7 = 11, plus 1 is 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\n2 + 1 = 3, plus 1 is 4. Write 4, no carry.\n\n0 + 0 = 0, plus 1 is 1. Write 1.\n\nSo the result is 422,064. Yep, same as before. So I think that's correct. \n\nWait, just to make sure, maybe adding the numbers in another way. Let's split 243,229 into 200,000 + 40,000 + 3,000 + 200 + 20 + 9. Then 178,835 into 100,000 + 70,000 + 8,000 + 800 + 30 + 5. Then