as 200,000 + 90,000 + 4,936, that's incorrect. Because 90,000 + 4,000 + 900 + 36 is 94,936, not 9,936. So that was a mistake. \n\nTherefore, my breakdown method was flawed. Let me correct that. \n\nSo, 204,857 is 200,000 + 4,000 + 800 + 50 + 7.\n\n294,936 is 200,000 + 90,000 + 4,000 + 900 + 36.\n\nAdding the 200,000 + 200,000 = 400,000.\n\n4,000 + 90,000 = 94,000.\n\n800 + 4,000 = 4,800.\n\n50 + 900 = 950.\n\n7 + 36 = 43.\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n400,000 + 94,000 = 494,000.\n\n494,000 + 4,800 = 498,800.\n\n498,800 + 950 = 499,750.\n\n499,750 + 43 = 499,793.\n\nAh, there we go. So that matches the first method. So the correct sum is 499,793. \n\nTherefore, my initial calculation was correct, and the breakdown method had an error in how I broke down the numbers. So the answer is 499,793. \n\nLet me verify using another method. Maybe adding the numbers digit by digit with more attention to carries. \n\nLet's write them vertically:\n\n  204,857\n+ 294,936\n________\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n7 + 6 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nNext digit (tens place): 5 + 3 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9. Write 9, no carry.\n\nNext digit (hundreds place): 8 + 9 = 17. Write 7, carry 1.\n\nNext digit (thousands place): 4 + 4 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9. Write 9, no carry.\n\nNext digit (ten-thousands place): 0 + 9 = 9. Write 9, no carry.\n\nNext digit (hundred-thousands place): 2 + 2 = 4. Write 4.\n\nSo the total is 499,793. \n\nYes, that's consistent. So the answer is 499,793. \n\nAlternatively, using a calculator to check. But since I don't have a calculator here, let me try another way. \n\nIf I subtract 204,857 from 500,000, what do I get? \n\n500,000 - 204,857. \n\n500,000 - 200,000 = 300,000.\n\n300,000 - 4,857 = 295,143. \n\nWait, 300,000 - 4,000 = 296,000.\n\n296,000 - 857 = 295,143. \n\nBut 295,143 is the difference. Therefore, 204,857 + 295,143 = 500,000. So 204,857 + 294,936 = 204,857 + (295,143 - 200) = 500,000 - 200 = 499,800. Wait, but that contradicts previous results. Wai