number is 299,071, which is 2 hundred thousands, 9 ten thousands, 9 thousands, 0 hundreds, 7 tens, 1 ones. So when aligned:\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 6 + 1 = 7\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 6 + 7 = 13 \u2192 3, carryover 1\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 8 + 0 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 2 + 9 = 11 \u2192 11, carryover 1\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 0 + 9 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carryover 1\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 8 + 2 = 10 + 1 = 11 \u2192 11, carryover 1\n\nBut since there are no more positions, we add the carryover 1 to the hundred thousands place. Wait, but the hundred thousands place in the first number is 8, and the second number has no digit there. So adding 8 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) = 10, plus carryover 1 = 11. So we write 1 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 1 to the millions place. So the millions place is 1. Therefore, the total is 1 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 7 (ones). So 1,029,377. But this contradicts the previous result of 1,101,937. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, let's check the addition again step by step:\n\nFirst number: 802,866\n\nSecond number: 299,071\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart with the ones place: 6 + 1 = 7\n\nTens place: 6 + 7 = 13 \u2192 3, carryover 1\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 0 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nThousands place: 2 + 9 = 11 \u2192 11, carryover 1\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 + 9 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carryover 1\n\nHundred-thousands place: 8 + 2 = 10 + 1 = 11 \u2192 11, carryover 1\n\nMillions place: 1 (carryover)\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nMillions: 1\n\nHundreds of thousands: 0\n\nTen thousands: 2\n\nThousands: 9\n\nHundreds: 3\n\nTens: 7\n\nOnes: 7\n\nWait, that would be 1,029,377. But when I added step by step before, I got 1,101,937. So which is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 802,866 + 299,071 using another method. Let's use the standard addition algorithm:\n\n      802,866\n\n    + 299,071\n\n    -----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n6 +