sult. So that checks out. \n\nAnother way: Maybe using another method like adding 176,748 + 498,700. Let's see, 176,748 + 500,000 would be 676,748, but since it's 498,700, which is 1,300 less than 500,000. So subtract 1,300 from 676,748. 676,748 - 1,000 = 675,748. Then subtract 300: 675,748 - 300 = 675,448. There we go, same answer. \n\nSo all methods lead to 675,448. I think that's correct. Let me just verify once more with column addition:\n\n176,748  \n+498,700  \n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 + 0 = 8  \n4 + 0 = 4  \n7 + 7 = 14 (carry 1)  \n6 + 8 = 14 + 1 = 15 (carry 1)  \n7 + 9 = 16 + 1 = 17 (carry 1)  \n1 + 4 = 5 + 1 = 6  \n\nSo the sum is 675,448. Yep, that's consistent. I think that's the right answer. No mistakes detected in the process. All methods converge to the same result. So I'm confident the answer is 675,448.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 176748 and 498700 is \\boxed{675448}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of 176,748 and 498,700, we align the numbers vertically and add each column starting from the rightmost digit:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n 176748 \\\\\n+498700 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n- Ones: \\(8 + 0 = 8\\)\n- Tens: \\(4 + 0 = 4\\)\n- Hundreds: \\(7 + 7 = 14\\) (carry over 1)\n- Thousands: \\(6 + 8 = 14 + 1 = 15\\) (carry over 1)\n- Ten-thousands: \\(7 + 9 = 16 + 1 = 17\\) (carry over 1)\n- Hundred-thousands: \\(1 + 4 = 5 + 1 = 6\\)\n\nPutting all the results together, the sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{675448}\n\\]",
