l is 1 followed by 8, then 4, 4, 1, 2. Wait, that would be 1,844,152. \n\nLet me check using another method to confirm. Maybe adding the numbers digit by digit another way.\n\n874,441\n+969,711\n= ?\n\nLet's break down both numbers into their components:\n\n874,441 is 800,000 + 70,000 + 4,000 + 400 + 40 + 1.\n\n969,711 is 900,000 + 60,000 + 9,000 + 700 + 10 + 1.\n\nAdding them together:\n\n800,000 + 900,000 = 1,700,000\n\n70,000 + 60,000 = 130,000\n\n4,000 + 9,000 = 13,000\n\n400 + 700 = 1,100\n\n40 + 10 = 50\n\n1 + 1 = 2\n\nNow add all those together:\n\n1,700,000 + 130,000 = 1,830,000\n\n1,830,000 + 13,000 = 1,843,000\n\n1,843,000 + 1,100 = 1,844,100\n\n1,844,100 + 50 = 1,844,150\n\n1,844,150 + 2 = 1,844,152\n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So the sum is 1,844,152. \n\nWait, but let me check once more with column addition to be absolutely sure.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1 + 1 = 2. Correct.\n\nTens: 4 + 1 = 5. Correct.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 1 = 5. Correct.\n\nThousands: 7 + 9 = 16. So 6, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nTen-thousands: 8 + 6 = 14. 14 + 1 (carryover) = 15. So 5, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nHundred-thousands: 8 + 9 = 17. 17 + 1 (carryover) = 18. So 8, carryover 1. Which becomes the millions place. So total is 1 (million), 8 (hundred-thousands), 4 (ten-thousands), 4 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 2 (ones). So 1,844,152. \n\nYes, that seems consistent. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using another approach: 874,441 + 969,711. Let's see, 874,441 + 900,000 = 1,774,441. Then add 69,711 to that. 1,774,441 + 60,000 = 1,834,441. Then add 9,711. 1,834,441 + 9,000 = 1,843,441. Then add 711: 1,843,441 + 700 = 1,844,141. Then add 11: 1,844,141 + 10 = 1,844,151. Then add 1: 1,844,152. \n\nSame result. So all methods lead to 1,844,152. Therefore, I can be confident that the sum is 1,844,152.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 874441 and 969711 is \\boxed{1844152}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of 874,441 and 969,711, we align the numbers vertically and add each column starting from the rightmost digit:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n 874441 \\\\\n+969711 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n1. Ones place: \\(1 + 1 = 2\\)\n2. Tens place: \\(4 + 1 = 5\\)\n3. Hundreds place: \\(4 + 1 = 5\\)\n4. Thousands place: \\(7 + 9 = 16\\) (write down 6, carry over 1)\n5. Ten-thousands place: \\(8 + 6 = 14\\) (add the carryover 1: \\(14 + 1 = 15\\), write down 5, carry over 1)\n6. Hundred-thousands place: \\(8 + 9 = 17\\) (add the carryover 1: \\(17 + 1 = 18\\), write down 8, carry over 1)\n\nThe final result is written as 1,844,152.\n\nTo verify, we can break down the numbers and add each component:\n- \\(800,000 + 900,000 = 1,700,000\\)\n- \\(70,000 + 60,000 = 130,000\\)\n- \\(4,000 + 9,000 = 13,000\\)\n- \\(400 + 700 = 1,100\\)\n- \\(40 + 10 = 50\\)\n- \\(1 + 1 = 2\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n- \\(1,700,000 + 130,000 = 1,830,000\\)\n- \\(1,830,000 + 13,000 = 1,843,000\\)\n- \\(1,843,000 + 1,100 = 1,844,100\\)\n- \\(1,844,100 + 50 = 1,844,150\\)\n- \\(1,844,150 + 2 = 1,844,152\\)\n\nThus, the sum of 874,441 and 969,711 is \\(\\boxed{1844152}\\).",
