 thousands) + 0 (hundred thousands) = 0, plus carryover 0 = 0. Write 0.\n\nSo the total is 675,347. But when I did the breakdown earlier, I thought I got 635,347. Wait, where did that come from?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check again. If 118,732 is 100,000 + 18,000 + 700 + 30 + 2, and 516,615 is 500,000 + 16,000 + 600 + 10 + 5, then adding those components:\n\n100,000 + 500,000 = 600,000\n\n18,000 + 16,000 = 34,000\n\n700 + 600 = 1,300\n\n30 + 10 = 40\n\n2 + 5 = 7\n\nAdding those: 600,000 + 34,000 = 634,000\n\n634,000 + 1,300 = 635,300\n\n635,300 + 40 = 635,340\n\n635,340 + 7 = 635,347.\n\nBut according to the column addition, it's 675,347. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the breakdown. Let me check the original numbers again. 118,732 + 516,615.\n\nWait, 118,732 is 1 hundred thousand, 1 ten thousand, 8 thousands, 7 hundreds, 3 tens, 2 ones.\n\n516,615 is 5 hundred thousands, 1 ten thousand, 6 thousands, 6 hundreds, 1 ten, 5 ones.\n\nSo when adding:\n\n1 hundred thousand + 5 hundred thousand = 6 hundred thousand.\n\n1 ten thousand + 1 ten thousand = 2 ten thousand.\n\n8 thousands + 6 thousands = 14 thousands.\n\n7 hundreds + 6 hundreds = 13 hundreds.\n\n3 tens + 1 ten = 4 tens.\n\n2 ones + 5 ones = 7 ones.\n\nSo that would be 6 hundred thousand, 2 ten thousand, 14 thousands, 13 hundreds, 4 tens, 7 ones.\n\nConvert that to numbers:\n\n6 hundred thousand = 600,000\n\n2 ten thousand = 20,000\n\n14 thousands = 14,000\n\n13 hundreds = 1,300\n\n4 tens = 40\n\n7 ones = 7\n\nAdding them up:\n\n600,000 + 20,000 = 620,000\n\n620,000 + 14,000 = 634,000\n\n634,000 + 1,300 = 635,300\n\n635,300 + 40 = 635,340\n\n635,340 + 7 = 635,347.\n\nBut according to the column addition, it's 675,347. So there's a conflict here. Which is correct?\n\nWait, this is impossible. There must be a miscalculation somewhere. Let me check with a calculator. Let's use an online calculator to verify.\n\n118,732 + 516,615.\n\nLet me compute 118,732 + 516,615.\n