r 1. Correct.\n\nThousands place: 6 + 3 = 9 + 1 = 10. So 0, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place: 0 + 5 = 5 + 1 = 6. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place: 8 + 5 = 13 + 1 = 14. So 4, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nMillions place: 1. Correct.\n\nSo vertical addition is correct. Then why does the breakdown give a different result?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check 806,900 + 553,981 again.\n\nWait, 806,900 + 553,981.\n\nWait, 806,900 is 800,000 + 6,900. 553,981 is 500,000 + 53,981. So adding 800,000 + 500,000 = 1,300,000. Then 6,900 + 53,981.\n\n6,900 + 53,981. Let's compute this again.\n\n6,900 + 53,981.\n\n6,900 + 50,000 = 56,900\n\n56,900 + 3,000 = 59,900\n\n59,900 + 981 = 60,881\n\nSo total is 1,300,000 + 60,881 = 1,360,881.\n\nBut according to vertical addition, it's 1,406,881. So there's a discrepancy of 46,000. That's a problem. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check the thousands place again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n806,900: thousands place is 6.\n\n553,981: thousands place is 3.\n\nAdding 6 + 3 = 9. Then add carryover 1 from hundreds place: 9 + 1 = 10. So thousands place is 0, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nHundreds place: 9 + 9 = 18. So 8, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nTens place: 0 + 8 = 8. Correct.\n\nOnes place: 0 + 1 = 1. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place: 0 + 5 = 5. Then add carryover 1: 6. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place: 8 + 5 = 13. Add carryover 1: 14. So 4, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nMillions place: 1. Correct.\n\nSo vertical addition is correct. Then why does the breakdown give a different result?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check 806,900 + 553,981 again.\n\nWait, 806,900 is 800,000 + 6,900. 553,981 is 500,000 + 53,981. So adding 800,000 + 500,000 = 1,300,000. Then 6,900 + 53,981.\n\n6,900 + 53,981. Let's compute this again.\n\n6,900 + 53,981.\n\n6,900 + 50,000 = 56,900\n\n56,900 + 3,000 = 59,900\n\n59,900 + 981 = 60,881\n\nSo total is 1,300,000 + 60,881 = 1,360,881.\n\nBut according to vertical addition, it's 1,406,881. So there's a difference of 46,000. That's a problem. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check the hundred thousands place.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n806,900: hundred thousands place is 8.\n\n553,981: hundred thousands place is 5.\n\nAdding 8 + 5 = 13. Then add carryover 1 from ten thousands place: 13 + 1 = 14. So hundred thousands place is 4, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nMillions place: carryover 1. Correct.\n\nSo vertical addition is correct. Then why does the breakdown give a different result?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check 806,900 + 553,981 again.\n\nWait, 806,900 is 800,000 + 6,900. 553,981 is 500,000 + 53,981. So adding 800,000 + 500,000 = 1,300,000. Then 6,900 + 53,981.\n\n6,900 + 53,981. Let's compute this again.\n\n6,900 + 53,981.\n\n6,900 + 50,000 = 56,900\n\n56,900 + 3,000 = 59,900\n\n59,900 + 981 = 60,881\n\nSo total is 1,300,000 + 60,881 = 1,360,881.\n\nBut according to vertical addition, it's 1,406,881. So there's a discrepancy of 46,000. That's a problem. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check the thousands place again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n806,900: thousands place is 6.\n\n553,981: thousands place is 3.\n\nAdding 6 + 3 = 9. Then add carryover 1 from hundreds place: 9 + 1 = 10. So thousands place is 0, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nHundreds place: 9 + 9 = 18. So 8, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nTens place: 0 + 8 = 8. Correct.\n\nOnes place: 0 + 1 = 1. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place: 0 + 5 = 5. Then add carryover 1: 6. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place: 8 + 5 = 13. Add carryover 1: 14. So 4, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nMillions place: 1. Correct.\n\nSo vertical addition is correct. Then why does the breakdown give a different result?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check 806,900 + 553,981 again.\n\nWait, 806,900 is 800,000 + 6,900. 55