ow, adding the two results: 1,300,000 + 66,408 = 1,366,408. Wait, that's different from what I got before. Hmm, so which one is correct?\n\nWait, hold on. Let me check the second method again. Maybe I messed up the breakdown.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n958,102: 900,000 + 58,102. Correct.\n\n408,306: 400,000 + 8,306. Correct.\n\nAdding 900,000 + 400,000 = 1,300,000. That's right.\n\n58,102 + 8,306. Let's compute that again.\n\n58,102 + 8,306:\n\nStart with the thousands: 58,102 has 50,000 and 8,102. 8,306 is 8,000 and 306.\n\nAdding 8,102 + 8,000 = 16,102\n\nThen 16,102 + 306 = 16,408\n\nWait, so 58,102 + 8,306 = 16,408\n\nThen total sum is 1,300,000 + 16,408 = 1,316,408\n\nWait, now I'm getting 1,316,408. But earlier I thought it was 1,366,408. So where did I go wrong?\n\nWait, let's check 58,102 + 8,306 again.\n\n58,102 + 8,306:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 + 6 = 8\n\nTens: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nHundreds: 1 + 3 = 4\n\nThousands: 8 + 8 = 16, carryover 1\n\nTen-thousands: 5 + 0 + 1 = 6\n\nSo, 64,408. Wait, that's 64,408. Then adding to 1,300,000:\n\n1,300,000 + 64,408 = 1,364,408.\n\nWait, now I'm confused. Let me do this step by step.\n\nFirst number: 958,102\n\nSecond number: 408,306\n\nAdding them:\n\nUnits place: 2 + 6 = 8\n\nTens place: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 3 = 4\n\nThousands place: 8 + 8 = 16. So write down 6, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 5 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 6\n\nHundred-thousands place: 9 + 4 = 13. So write down 3, carryover 1. But since there are no more places, it's 13.\n\nSo total is 136,608. But when I broke it down into 900,000 + 400,000 = 1,300,000 and 58,102 + 8,306 = 64,408, then 1,300,000 + 64,408 = 1,364,408. Wait, that's conflicting.\n\nWait, so which is correct? There must be a mistake here. Let me check the breakdown again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n958,102: 900,000 + 58,102. Correct.\n\n408,306: 400,000 + 8,306. Correct.\n\nAdding 900,000 + 400,000 = 1,300,000. Correct.\n\nNow, 58,102 + 8,306. Let's compute this:\n\n58,102 + 8,306:\n\nStart with 58,102 + 8,000 = 66,102\n\nThen 66,102 + 306 = 66,408\n\nWait, so 58,102 + 8,306 = 66,408. Then 1,300,000 + 66,408 = 1,366,408.\n\nBut when adding directly, we get 136,608. There's a discrepancy here. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the breakdown. Let me check the original numbers again.\n\nWait, 958,102 is 9 hundred fifty-eight thousand one hundred two. 408,306 is four hundred eight thousand three hundred six. Adding them:\n\n958,102 + 408,306.\n\nLet me use another method. Let's add the numbers digit by digit:\n\nFirst number: 9 5 8 1 0 2\n\nSecond number: 4 0 8 3 0 6\n\nAdding from right to left:\n\n2 + 6 = 8 (ones place)\n\n0 + 0 = 0 (tens place)\n\n1 + 3 = 4 (hundreds place)\n\n8 + 8 = 16, write down 6, carryover 1 (thousands place)\n\n5 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 6 (ten-thousands place)\n\n9 + 4 = 13, write down 3, carryover 1 (hundred-thousands place). So total is 136,608.\n\nBut when I broke it down into 900,000 + 400,000 = 1,300,000 and 58,102 + 8,306 = 66,408, then 1,300,000 + 66,408 = 1,366,408. Wait, that's different. So why is there a discrepancy?\n\nAh! Wait a second. The second number is 408,306. If I break it into 400,000 + 8,306, that's correct. But 400,000 + 8,306 is 408,306. Then 958,102 + 408,306 is (900,000 + 58,102) + (400,000 + 8,306) = 1,300,000 + 66,408 = 1,366,408. But according to the direct addition, it's 136,608. So which is correct?\n\nWait, this is a problem. There must be a miscalculation here. Let me check the addition step by step again.\n\nFirst, adding 958,102 and 408,306.\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n  958,102\n\n+ 408,306\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n2 + 6 = 8 (ones place)\n\n0 + 0 = 0 (tens place)\n\n1 + 3 = 4 (hundreds place)\n\n8 + 8 = 16, write down 6, carryover 1 (thousands place)\n\n5 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 6 (ten-thousands place)\n\n9 + 4 = 13, write down 3, carryover 1 (hundred-thousands place). So total is 136,608.\n\nBut when I broke down the numbers:\n\n958,102 = 900,000 + 58,102\n\n408,306 = 400,000 + 8,306\n\nAdding 900,000 + 400,000 = 1,300,000\n\n58,102 + 8,306 = ?\n\n58,102 + 8,306:\n\nLet's compute this:\n\n58,102 + 8,306:\n\nStart with 58,102 + 8,000 = 66,102\n\n66,102 + 306 = 66,408\n\nThen 1,300,000 + 66,408 = 1,366,408\n\nWait, so which is correct? There's a conflict here. The direct addition gives 136,608, but breaking into 1,300,000 + 66,408 gives 1,366,408. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check 58,102 + 8,306 again.\n\n58,102 + 8,306:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 + 6 = 8\n\nTens: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nHundreds: 1 + 3 = 4\n\nThousands: 8 + 8 = 16, so 6 with carryover 1\n\nTen-thousands: 5 + 0 + 1 = 6\n\nHundred-thousands: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nSo, 64,408. Wait, that's 64,408. Then 1,300,000 + 64,408 = 1,364,408. But that's even different.\n\nWait, now I'm really confused. Let me check with another method. Let's use the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nFirst number: 958,102\n\nSecond number: 408,306\n\nAdding them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 6 = 8 (ones place)\n\n0 + 0 = 0 (tens place)\n\n1 + 3 = 4 (hundreds place)\n\n8 + 8 = 16, write 6, carryover 1 (thousands place)\n\n5 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 6 (ten-thousands place)\n\n9 + 4 = 13, write 3, carryover 1 (hundred-thousands place). So total is 136,608.\n\nBut when I broke down 958,102 into 900,000 + 58,102 and 408,306 into 400,000 + 8,306, adding those gives 1,300,000 + 66,408 = 1,366,408. So why is there a discrepancy?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the breakdown. Let me check 58,102 + 8,306 again.\n\nWait, 58,102 + 8,306:\n\n58,102 is 50,000 + 8,102\n\n8,306 is 8,000 + 306\n\nAdding 50,000 + 8,000 = 58,000\n\n8,102 + 306 = 8,408\n\nSo total is 58,000 + 8,408 = 66,408. Then 1,300,000 + 66,408 = 1,366,408.\n\nBut according to direct addition, it's 136,608. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe the problem is in the breakdown. Let me check the original numbers again.\n\nWait, 958,102 + 408,306.\n\nWait, 958,102