,339,722\n\n1,339,722 + 19 = 1,339,741\n\nYes, that matches. So, the sum is indeed 1,339,741. I think that's correct. Let me just do a quick check with another method, maybe using another addition strategy.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the fact that 716,122 + 623,619 is the same as (700,000 + 600,000) + (16,122 + 23,619). Let's compute each part:\n\n700,000 + 600,000 = 1,300,000\n\n16,122 + 23,619. Let's add those:\n\n16,122 + 20,000 = 36,122\n\n36,122 + 3,000 = 39,122\n\n39,122 + 600 = 39,722\n\n39,722 + 19 = 39,741\n\nNow, add 1,300,000 + 39,741 = 1,339,741. Yep, same result. So, definitely 1,339,741. I think that's solid. No mistakes detected in the process. All methods lead to the same answer. So, I'm confident that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 716122 and 623619 is \\boxed{1339741}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of 716,122 and 623,619, we align the numbers and add digit by digit from right to left:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n 716122 \\\\\n+623619 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n- Ones place: \\(2 + 9 = 11\\) (write down 1, carry over 1)\n- Tens place: \\(2 + 1 = 3 + 1 = 4\\)\n- Hundreds place: \\(1 + 6 = 7\\)\n- Thousands place: \\(6 + 3 = 9\\)\n- Ten-thousands place: \\(7 + 2 = 9\\)\n- Hundred-thousands place: \\(7 + 6 = 13\\) (write down 3, carry over 1)\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is \\(1,339,741\\).\n\nVerification by breaking down the addition:\n- \\(716,122 + 600,000 = 1,316,122\\)\n- \\(1,316,122 + 23,619 = 1,339,741\\)\n\nAnother verification by splitting the numbers:\n- \\(700,000 + 600,000 = 1,300,000\\)\n- \\(16,122 + 23,619 = 39,741\\)\n- \\(1,300,000 + 39,741 = 1,339,741\\)\n\nThus, the sum of 716,122 and 623,619 is \\(\\boxed{1339741}\\).",
